/-  H1000Line_All.lean -- `hLine` of ALL 25 bands of the height-1000 segment, and the ladder
    statement from the remaining inputs only
    (GENERATED by telperion/examples/zeta_reflection/emit_h1000_line.py; do not edit).

    * `seg_lineHyp`   : `(BandGlue_h1000.seg i).LineHyp` for every `i < 25` (bands `H1000Line_B00..B24`).
    * `lineHyp_of_edges` : the same `hLine` for ANY `BandGlue.BandData` with the segment band's
                        `T0`, `T1`, `n` (so an integration stage may re-choose the enclosure
                        data of a band, e.g. wider kernel-provable boxes, and keep this `hLine`).
    * `all_nontrivial_zeros_up_to_height_1000_of_certs` : the same statement by the certificate route
                        (any band data with the same `T0`, `T1`, `n`, its own enclosures and pins).
    * `all_nontrivial_zeros_up_to_height_1000_of_offline` : the height-1000 ladder statement with
                        `hLine` (here) and `hγ` (`HeightFloor.height_floor`) discharged; the only
                        remaining inputs are, per band, the two edge-clearance slabs and the five
                        RvM enclosures (`BandGlue.BandData.ReducedInputs` minus `LineHyp`).
    * `segWith_valid` : `BandGlue.BandData.Valid` for band `i` with ANY enclosures `E` satisfying
                        the two pins (`H1000Glue.PinOk`).
    * `all_nontrivial_zeros_up_to_height_1000_of_encl` : THE INTEGRATION TARGET -- the ladder
                        statement from, per band, enclosure data `E i`, its pins, its five
                        enclosures, and the edge-clearance slabs (49 of them: band 0's lower
                        slab is discharged by the height floor, `H1000Glue.slab0_band0`).
    Axioms [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound] (AxiomGuardH1000Line.lean); no `sorry`.
    conjecture1_proved = False.
-/
